   "he": "וְכוֹתֵב סֵפֶר תּוֹרָה לִשְׁמוֹ. תְּנָא: וּבִלְבַד שֶׁלֹּא יִתְנָאֶה בְּשֶׁל אֲבוֹתָיו.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the king «writes a Torah scroll for his sake.» The Sages «taught» in a baraita (Tosefta 4:4): The king fulfills the mitzva «provided that he does not beautify himself with» the Torah scroll «of his ancestors» for this purpose, i.e., he must write his own scroll."
